<title>UK: Siemens eyes joint venture with Westinghouse-paper.</title>
<headline>Siemens eyes joint venture with Westinghouse-paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-French power-generating equipment manufacturer GEC-ALSTHOM is in a contest with its German rival Siemens to form a joint venture with U.S. group Westinghouse, according to a report in The Sunday Times.</p>
<p>The report said Siemens was the clear frontrunner to secure a deal that would link its turbine manufacturing business with Westinghouse.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7718</p>
